md("""## 3. `--mode` (required): pick the engine composition

The one option you cannot omit. Three choices:

- `fast` - QEMU only. Functional, full speed. No cycle count.
- `cycle` - one cycle-accurate vsim engine, from reset. Accurate, but slow.
- `hybrid` - QEMU fast-forwards to your region of interest (ROI), then vsim measures just that window. Fast *and* accurate where it matters.

An analogy for travel: `fast` is a plane (quick, no detail of the road), `cycle` is walking the whole way (every step counted), `hybrid` is flying to the city then walking only the one street you care about.

**Demo - `fast`:** the portable `vplat_hello.elf` prints and exits.""")

code("!andesim run --mode fast tests/fixtures/vplat_hello.elf", FAST_DEMO)

md("**Error - forget `--mode`:** the driver tells you the one thing it cannot guess.")
code("!andesim run tests/fixtures/vplat_hello.elf", ERR_NO_MODE)

md("""## 4. `--engine`: choose which simulator

`fast` always uses QEMU, so you rarely set `--engine` there. For `cycle` / `hybrid` you pick one vsim engine by id (from `list engines`). If only one cycle engine exists it is the default; if **more than one** exists, you must choose.

**Demo - name an engine for a `cycle` run** (this one really runs vsim, so it takes a few seconds):""")

code("!andesim run --mode cycle --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium tests/fixtures/vplat_hello.elf", CYCLE_DEMO)

